<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 174 bln lire of Italy Cct.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 174 bln lire of Italy Cct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 174 billion lire of seven-year variable-rate certificates (CCT) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 450 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 8.287 trillion lire at the open auction for the January 1, 2004 paper, against 4.5 trillion lire worth of paper on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 99.65 from 100.00 at the previous CCT sale on February 13.</p>
</text>
